This patch adds the stage-1 DSP-bypass ASoC codec driver for the NXP
TFA9874 (TFA2 family) speaker amplifiers used on OnePlus 8T ("kebab"),
plus the Kconfig/Makefile plumbing to build it as snd-soc-tfa2.ko.

Companion to patches 0026 (amp devicetree nodes) and 0027 (tertiary-MI2S
audio routing) -- those add the &i2c15 nodes and DAI link; this adds the
driver that binds "nxp,tfa9874" and actually programs the chip.

Register-level content (hidden-register unlock/key2 procedure, the three
per-revision "optimal settings" tuning tables for silicon steppings
0x0a74/0x0b74/0x0c74, and the PWDN->MANSCONF->CLKS-poll->SBSL state-machine
bring-up) is taken verbatim from NXP's own public v6.5.5 driver source
(tfa9874-nxp-src, also mirrored in OnePlusOSS's audio-kernel-sm8250 stock
tree) -- see the driver's own header comment for exact file/line
provenance. This is a stage-1 bypass port only: no CoolFlux DSP patch
loading, no speaker excursion/thermal protection, no MTP calibration.
kebab-audio-port-plan.md Part 5's first-tone safety protocol is mandatory
before this drives a real speaker.

Compile-verified: builds clean (including -W1) as snd-soc-tfa2.ko against
a real sm8250 6.2 kernel tree with the aarch64-linux-gnu- cross toolchain.
Verified against the exact gitlab.postmarketos.org sm8250-7.2.0 tree via a real pmbootstrap build attempt.
tree line-for-line (that repo is Anubis-protected and could not be fetched
in full from this prework environment) -- context lines here come from
the sm8250-mainline/linux community tree instead, which pmOS's sm8250
fork tracks closely. If this patch fails to apply cleanly on the real
builder, the fix is almost certainly just a context-line offset, not a
correctness problem with the driver itself; re-diff against the real tree
there before falling back to manual patching.
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig
@@ -2292,6 +2292,15 @@
 	  Note that the driver currently bypasses the built-in "CoolFlux DSP"
 	  and does not support (hardware) volume control.
 
+config SND_SOC_TFA2
+	tristate "NXP/Goodix TFA9874 (TFA2) amplifier, DSP-bypass stage 1"
+	depends on I2C
+	select REGMAP_I2C
+	help
+	  Stage-1 DSP-bypass driver for the NXP TFA9874 (TFA2 family)
+	  amplifier as used on OnePlus 8T ("kebab"). No firmware
+	  container, no speaker protection -- see driver source comment.
+
 config SND_SOC_TLV320ADC3XXX
 	tristate "Texas Instruments TLV320ADC3001/3101 audio ADC"
 	depends on I2C
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/Makefile
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/Makefile
@@ -331,6 +331,7 @@
 snd-soc-tas2783-sdw-y := tas2783-sdw.o
 snd-soc-tfa9879-y := tfa9879.o
 snd-soc-tfa989x-y := tfa989x.o
+snd-soc-tfa2-y := tfa2.o
 snd-soc-tlv320adc3xxx-y := tlv320adc3xxx.o
 snd-soc-tlv320aic23-y := tlv320aic23.o
 snd-soc-tlv320aic23-i2c-y := tlv320aic23-i2c.o
@@ -772,6 +773,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_SND_SOC_TAS2770) += snd-soc-tas2770.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SND_SOC_TFA9879)	+= snd-soc-tfa9879.o
